.bd
SUBROUTINE(S)
.in +5
.br
.bd
getgrent, getgrgid, getgrnam, setgrent, endgrent
- get group file entry
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
C
.in +5
.br
.bd
#include <grp.h>
.sp
.bd
struct group *getgrent()
.sp
.bd 2
struct group *getgrgid(gid)
.br
int gid;
.sp
.bd 2
struct group *getgrnam(name)
.br
char *name;
.sp
.bd
int setgrent()
.sp
.bd
int endgrent()
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
DESCRIPTIONS
.in +5
.br
Each of the "get" routines -
.bd
getgrent, getgrgid
and
.bd
getgrnam
- returns a pointer to an object with the following structure:
.sp
.in +8
.nf
.bd 7
    struct group
        {
	char	*gr_name;
	char	*gr_passwd;
	int	gr_gid;
	char	**gr_mem;
        }
.sp
.fi
.in -8
Each pointer contains the broken-out fields of a line in the group
file.
.sp
The
.bd
gr_mem
field is an array of pointers to the member names, terminated by a
null pointer.  A group with no members gives an array whose first
element is the null pointer.  As with the other fields it points
into a static area that the next call overwrites.
.sp
Unlike
.bd
struct passwd
in
.bd
getpwent (3),
the group id here is an
.bd
int
and not a single byte.  The password file and the
.bd
chown
system call have room for a one-byte group id; the group file does
not, and holds the number in full.
.sp
.in +5
.bd
getgrent
- reads the next line in the file; it will open the file, if
necessary.
.sp
.bd
setgrent
- rewinds the file
.sp
.bd
endgrent
- closes the file
.sp
.bd
getgrgid
- searches from the beginning of the file until a matching group
ID is found, or until an end of file is encountered.
.sp
.bd
getgrnam
- searches from the beginning of the file until a matching name is
found, or until an end of file is encountered.
.sp 2
.in 0
.in 5
.bd
ERRORS
.in +5
.br
A zero (NULL pointer) is returned upon an error or at end of file.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
NOTES
.in +5
.br
All information to be saved should be copied since it is contained
only in a temporary area.
.sp
A line with too few fields, or one longer than the buffer the
routine reads into, is skipped rather than returned.  A group with
more than 31 members has the surplus ignored.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
FILES
.in +5
.br
/etc/group
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
ALSO READ
.in +5
